{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question","id":1190646,"title":"Inflict damage stunt question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-01T07:01:04-08:00","id":1190646,"title":"Inflict damage stunt question","content":"Hey guys!<br /> <br /> I got one more question about scion origin rules, i looked over the 101combat simulation on post, but i didnt fine anything to cohoborate on book so here is the question.<br /> <br /> After overcome the target defenses with sucess we can apply stunts, I can apply the same stunt in the same attack more the one time?<br /> <br /> Example: spend two sucess on inflict damage stunt to take out a opponent faster or something like that? Or the only way to give two inflict damage is via critical hit with 4S?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T07:33:43-08:00","id":1190659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question#post1190646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys!<br /> <br /> I got one more question about scion origin rules, i looked over the 101combat simulation on post, but i didnt fine anything to cohoborate on book so here is the question.<br /> <br /> After overcome the target defenses with sucess we can apply stunts, I can apply the same stunt in the same attack more the one time?<br /> <br /> Example: spend two sucess on inflict damage stunt to take out a opponent faster or something like that? Or the only way to give two inflict damage is via critical hit with 4S?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only do each stunt one time. So yea, 1 injury its 1 success and for 2 injuries its 5 successes due to the cost of buying both stunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T08:33:16-08:00","id":1190676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190659#post1190659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can only do each stunt one time. So yea, 1 injury its 1 success and for 2 injuries its 5 successes due to the cost of buying both stunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see thanks!<br /> <br /> Do you know how to proced if the oponent ir\u00e1 not aware of the danger, like a sniper at long range shooting a chatacter, he should roll for defense ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T12:47:43-08:00","id":1190750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190676#post1190676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see thanks!<br /> <br /> Do you know how to proced if the oponent ir\u00e1 not aware of the danger, like a sniper at long range shooting a chatacter, he should roll for defense ?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far it's looking like you always use defense. The only sense of it you can make for ambushes is &quot;something something something mythology&quot; or &quot;something something something fate&quot;. Maybe that will get clarified in the cleaned up version of Origin we get eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:07:58-08:00","id":1190784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190750#post1190750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So far it's looking like you always use defense. The only sense of it you can make for ambushes is &amp;quot;something something something mythology&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;something something something fate&amp;quot;. Maybe that will get clarified in the cleaned up version of Origin we get eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope their clarify that for now i will house rule making the target with only difficult 1 on that,if i do it this will be a let down for one of players, he rolls a ninja style character.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:12:42-08:00","id":1190835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190676#post1190676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see thanks!<br /> <br /> Do you know how to proced if the oponent ir\u00e1 not aware of the danger, like a sniper at long range shooting a chatacter, he should roll for defense ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ambush<br /> Sometimes, the best way to win is before your opponent even knows there is a fight. When attempting to surprise someone, the ambushers roll Agility + Dexterity vs. the opponent\u2019s Integrity + Cunning to represent sneaking up on them. Players can also make a case for different dice pools if the situation calls for it, such as Empathy + Cunning to distract an opponent, or to convince them that the ambusher is harmless before the attack.<br /> If a group is trying to surprise another group, pool the successes on both sides and divide them by the number of people on each side (round down).<br /> The target\u2019s roll becomes the Difficulty for the ambusher. After the ambusher overcomes the Difficulty, she may spend any remaining successes on the following effect:<br /> Surprise (Variable): Impose a Complication on the Initiative roll for the opposing team by one for each success spent. If anyone on the opposing team cannot buy off the Complication on their initiative roll, then they do not get an action on the first turn of combat.<br /> <br /> Some of those pools obviously need to be cleaned up because intergrity and such don't exist, but basically roll the most appropriate pool for the nature of the ambush, if you win they can't act in round one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T17:26:36-08:00","id":1190858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190835#post1190835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those pools obviously need to be cleaned up because intergrity and such don't exist, but basically roll the most appropriate pool for the nature of the ambush, if you win they can't act in round one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Integrity <i>does</i> in fact exist. There was an updated version of the Origin book released on January 27th rather than the 25th which cleaned a few things up. Integrity is a skill in it.<br /> <br /> Now <i>agility</i> doesn't exist, so-<br /> <br /> Edit: Anywho, it looks like the benefit of a sneak attack is mostly in the form of your opponent not attacking, but they can still defend, from my read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T19:38:50-08:00","id":1190886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190858#post1190858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Integrity <i>does</i> in fact exist. There was an updated version of the Origin book released on January 27th rather than the 25th which cleaned a few things up. Integrity is a skill in it.<br /> <br /> Now <i>agility</i> doesn't exist, so-<br /> <br /> Edit: Anywho, it looks like the benefit of a sneak attack is mostly in the form of your opponent not attacking, but they can still defend, from my read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah thats whats looks like, but it dont make sense if you dont know you are being attacked you cant defendcin first place, yeah in scion we can presume the fate can help then to see that comming in the last minute, but of the ambusher is a scion of Loki? Or some sneak and trick god? Fate should help to cloak then aswell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T19:48:41-08:00","id":1190887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190886#post1190886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah thats whats looks like, but it dont make sense if you dont know you are being attacked you cant defendcin first place, yeah in scion we can presume the fate can help then to see that comming in the last minute, but of the ambusher is a scion of Loki? Or some sneak and trick god? Fate should help to cloak then aswell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well a couple of things to note... Most opponents don't roll defense, they have a flat defense. <br /> <br /> And if say, the PC is firing from another building using a military sniper rifle, I'd probably assign some Enhancement (3 or so?) on the attack due to superior gear and positioning.<br /> <br /> And if the target is some mortal with no combat training, I may handwave that if they make the hit then they succeed on the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T04:24:08-08:00","id":1190939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190887#post1190887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well a couple of things to note... Most opponents don't roll defense, they have a flat defense. <br /> <br /> And if say, the PC is firing from another building using a military sniper rifle, I'd probably assign some Enhancement (3 or so?) on the attack due to superior gear and positioning.<br /> <br /> And if the target is some mortal with no combat training, I may handwave that if they make the hit then they succeed on the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey you got some good ideas, i was too much focused on \u201cmake sense of things\u201d, a enchancement bonus will do, thanks man!<br /> <br /> I was just wandering, my group and i was used to play world of darkness material, so we always think on player vs player situation, but I believe scion theme is not that( after all you need player permission to do a lot things), and we should just focus on the heroism, I can see a good old fashioned epic adventure comming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T06:24:51-08:00","id":1190958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190939#post1190939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey you got some good ideas, i was too much focused on \u201cmake sense of things\u201d, a enchancement bonus will do, thanks man!<br /> <br /> I was just wandering, my group and i was used to play world of darkness material, so we always think on player vs player situation, but I believe scion theme is not that( after all you need player permission to do a lot things), and we should just focus on the heroism, I can see a good old fashioned epic adventure comming.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it were PvP I may allow, say, a Cunning + Firearms to notice the sniper gleam from the scope or whatever, potentially helping alleviate the surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 03-03-2018, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T17:23:23-08:00","id":1191484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thiagocord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1190886#post1190886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah thats whats looks like, but it dont make sense if you dont know you are being attacked you cant defendcin first place, yeah in scion we can presume the fate can help then to see that comming in the last minute, but of the ambusher is a scion of Loki? Or some sneak and trick god? Fate should help to cloak then aswell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you could probably just use the threshold stunts from page 74. Use any extra success from the opposed ambush roll to give yourself enhancements on the attack and give them complications on their defense roll because in addition to the first attack you have things lined up and hit them totally unawares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T06:45:29-08:00","id":1191607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1190646-inflict-damage-stunt-question?p=1191484#post1191484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, you could probably just use the threshold stunts from page 74. Use any extra success from the opposed ambush roll to give yourself enhancements on the attack and give them complications on their defense roll because in addition to the first attack you have things lined up and hit them totally unawares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was used to storytelling system so I think I look the situation 